# Why this file exists: prettier does not honour a nested package's
# .prettierignore when it is invoked from the repo root (which is how the CI
# quality gate runs: `npx prettier --check .`). Without this file the root
# gate checked files that packages/core exempts in its own gate
# (`cd packages/core && npm run format:check`), so the two gates disagreed
# and CI showed red on files the package gate considers out of scope.
#
# Policy: this ignore mirrors packages/core/.prettierignore exactly — its
# core-owned .js/.mjs exemption, its artifact directories, and its entry for
# the generated braid.* schema — and nothing more. Do not widen it into a
# blanket *.js/*.mjs ignore: .js/.mjs files outside packages/core
# (packages/providers, packages/telegram, packages/contrib) are
# prettier-clean and stay checked by the root gate.

# Core-owned .js/.mjs: mirrors the package-level exemption in
# packages/core/.prettierignore so both gates treat these paths the same.
packages/core/**/*.js
packages/core/**/*.mjs

# Build, coverage, and scratch artifacts (same set as packages/core).
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
.tmp/
.eslintcache

# Generated braid.* schema (packages/core/.prettierignore carries the same
# entry): the generator's output is the canonical form and
# check-braid-schema.mjs byte-compares against it, so prettier must not
# rewrite the artifact.
packages/core/schema/braid.schema.json
